# Backend Python

## Layering

- `app/routes/api.py` — thin handlers, `jsonify()`, no vendor HTTP
- `app/services/` — business logic
- `app/clients/` — HTTP clients (SEC, Stooq); no Flask imports
- `app/repositories.py` — SQL only; upserts with `ON CONFLICT`
- `app/workers/` — job handlers; drain `ingestion_jobs`

## Required patterns

```python
# SEC: Host header must match URL host (www.sec.gov vs data.sec.gov)
response = session.get(url, headers=client.headers_for(url))

# Admin errors: JSON body, not bare 500
return jsonify({"error": str(exc)}), 500
```

## Data rules

- Multiple tickers can share one CIK — `companies.cik` is not unique.
- Request-time routes read SQLite first; Nasdaq only as optional fallback.
- Long ETL (feeds, SEC bulk) belongs in worker jobs or bootstrap, not blocking reads.

## Queries & performance

- No N+1 patterns: batch reads in repositories; never query per ticker/row inside route handlers or loops.
- **Run `EXPLAIN QUERY PLAN` before AND after** any new `SELECT` on `companies`, `articles`, or `metrics`, any new join, any new `ORDER BY`/`GROUP BY`, or any filter on an un-indexed column. Record the plan in the Phase 4 outcome summary.
- Benchmark wall-clock timing with representative row counts when adding queries to hot paths (screener load, article feed, scoring pipeline).
- Do not add materialized-cache tables or snapshot stores without measured need — SQLite-first simplicity.

## Prohibited patterns

| Pattern | Reason |
|---------|--------|
| Per-row DB call in a loop | N+1; use batch repository reads |
| Hardcoded scoring thresholds in route handlers | Breaks canonical scoring architecture |
| Schema field names invented without inspection | Hallucinated fields cause silent data corruption |
| `print()` in production paths | Use structured logging (`logging.info/warning/error`) |
| New ingestion source without idempotency guard | Causes duplicate DB writes on rerun |
| New SQLite table without migration + index plan | Schema drift; unindexed table scans |

## Metrics & scoring

- Canonical logic: `metric_registry.py`, `scoring.py`, `metrics_engine.py` — not ad-hoc formulas in routes or repositories.
- API responses expose computed scores; frontend must not re-implement composites.
- Scoring changes: run `test_scoring.py`, `test_metrics_engine.py`; see `scripts/validate_scores.py` for golden tickers.

## Tests

- Fixtures: `app`, `client` from `app/tests/conftest.py`
- Mock HTTP; no live SEC/Stooq in unit tests
- Run: `python -m pytest app/tests/ -q`
